  "rationale": "Both answers are valid for the stated sense, but the national split is materially overstated: authoritative Malaysian references explicitly equate “tahun depan” with “tahun hadapan” and state that both forms may be used. The relation should not be different-common-word. No false-friend contrast is needed.",
  "claim_reviews": [
    {
      "subject": "English cue and sense",
      "conclusion": "“Next year” correctly matches “the calendar year immediately after this one.”",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://repositori.kemendikdasmen.go.id/16351/1/Tata%20Bahasa%20Baku%20Bahasa%20Ind.pdf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Indonesian answer: tahun depan",
      "conclusion": "Correct and ordinary Indonesian wording for the intended temporal sense.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://repositori.kemendikdasmen.go.id/16351/1/Tata%20Bahasa%20Baku%20Bahasa%20Ind.pdf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Malaysian answer: tahun hadapan",
      "conclusion": "Correct Malaysian Malay wording for the intended sense, but it is not exclusive; Malaysian references also recognize “tahun depan.”",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=73980&keyword=hadap",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=175768&keyword=taklimat"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Final relation and national split",
      "conclusion": "“different-common-word” is materially inaccurate or overstated. DBP explicitly gives “tahun depan” as equivalent to “tahun hadapan” and says both can be used, so this is better treated as shared wording with a possible Malaysian preference for “tahun hadapan.”",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=73980&keyword=hadap",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=175768&keyword=taklimat"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "False-friend contrast",
      "conclusion": "No false-friend contrast is required. “Depan” and “hadapan” can also refer to physical front/forward position, but in “tahun depan/tahun hadapan” both function transparently as temporal expressions; the empty contrast field is not misleading.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=73980&keyword=depan",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=175768&keyword=hadapan"
      ]
    }
